<div class="paragraph" style="text-align: center; font-style: italic; color: var(--section-num); margin: 2rem 0 1rem;">
  Related to the above:
</div>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<!-- Section 18                                      -->
<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="section-number">§ 18</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And for this reason, it is forbidden to eat any [new] grain before the <span class="heb-term">Omer</span>. For we need to draw down our livelihood and our eating through the <span class="heb-term">emunah</span> of Providence alone — which is the aspect of seeing, through which the <span class="heb-term">shefa</span> is drawn down in measure, in boundary and in time, as mentioned above. And this is what we merit through the waving of the <span class="heb-term">Omer</span>, as mentioned above.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  But before the <span class="heb-term">Omer</span>, the <span class="heb-term">klipos</span> still have a hold on the <span class="heb-term">shefa</span> — these <span class="heb-term">klipos</span> that are drawn from excess of light, and which have a hold on the <span class="heb-term">shefa</span> through the sin of Adam HaRishon [the first man], who blemished the <span class="heb-term">emunah</span>, as is explained elsewhere. And this is the aspect of: <span class="verse">"In sorrow you shall eat of it… by the sweat of your brow you shall eat bread"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Genesis 3:17, 19)</span>, etc. For all of this is because of the hold of the <span class="heb-term">klipos</span> that intensify through the heresies that come through the aspect of excess of light — through wanting to investigate His greatness, blessed be He, as mentioned above.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And therefore, Israel cannot eat any [new] grain until they remove it from the hold of the <span class="heb-term">klipos</span>, which are the aspect of heresies. And therefore, it is forbidden to eat <span class="heb-term">chadash</span> <span class="heb-def">[new grain]</span> until the <span class="heb-term">Omer</span> is offered. For then we bind all the six directions to Hashem, blessed be He, and complete Providence is drawn in <span class="heb-term">ratzo vashuv</span>, in the aspect of seeing. Through this, a vessel is made — the aspect of boundary and time — to receive the <span class="heb-term">shefa</span> in a measured, gradual manner. And the hold of the heresies and the <span class="heb-term">klipos</span> on the <span class="heb-term">shefa</span> is annulled. And then specifically, the new [grain] is permitted — for then we receive the <span class="heb-term">shefa</span> through the path of holiness alone, by making vessels and measure through the waving of the <span class="heb-term">Omer</span>, as mentioned above.
</div>

